{"name":"Wild Horses","hex":"#8d6747","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wild horses","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of wild horse","A force not subject to human control and normally stronger than a man."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wild_horses"}],"entries":[{"title":"Przewalski's horse","blocks":[{"text":"Przewalski's horse, also called the takhi, Mongolian wild horse or Dzungarian horse, is a rare and endangered wild horse originally native to the steppes of Central Asia. It is named after the Russian geographer and explorer Nikolay Przhevalsky. Once extinct in the wild, since the 1990s it has been reintroduced to its native habitat in Mongolia in the Hustai National Park, Takhin Tal Nature Reserve, Khomiin Tal, and several other locales in Central Asia and Eastern Europe."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Przewalskis_horse_02.jpg/330px-Przewalskis_horse_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Przewalski's_horse"},{"title":"Tarpan","blocks":[{"text":"The tarpan was a free-ranging horse population of the western Eurasian steppe which was first documented in the 18th century and went extinct in the early 20th century."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Kherson_tarpan.jpg/330px-Kherson_tarpan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tarpan"},{"title":"Wild Horses (Rolling Stones song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Wild Horses\" is a song by the English rock band the Rolling Stones from their 1971 album Sticky Fingers. It was also released on 12 June 1971 as a single, with \"Sway\" as its B-side. However, The Flying Burrito Brothers were the first to release the song nearly a year earlier in April 1970, with a cover appearing on their second album."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/22/Wild_Horses_by_The_Rolling_Stones_Japanese_vinyl.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wild_Horses_(Rolling_Stones_song)"},{"title":"Wild Horses (Gino Vannelli song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Wild Horses\" is a song by Canadian singer-songwriter Gino Vannelli. Vannelli came up with the track's basis during a trip to Santa Fe, New Mexico, to meet a shaman. He co-wrote the lyrics with Roy Freeland and produced it with his brothers, Joe and Ross Vannelli. The song is about a man who promises never to leave his partner no matter what they experience together. It was included on Vannelli's ninth studio album, Big Dreamers Never Sleep, and released as its lead single in 1987."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c2/Wild_Horses_Gino_Vannelli_cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wild_Horses_(Gino_Vannelli_song)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Equus_ferus_distribution.png/330px-Equus_ferus_distribution.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Equus_ferus_distribution.png/330px-Equus_ferus_distribution.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEquus_ferus_distribution.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Portrait_of_Przewalski%27s_Horse.jpg/500px-Portrait_of_Przewalski%27s_Horse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Portrait_of_Przewalski%27s_Horse.jpg/1280px-Portrait_of_Przewalski%27s_Horse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7